        <h4 style="font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">1. Why was my PDF rejected by the GATE GOAPS portal even though it was below 200KB?</h4>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
          Rejection on the GOAPS portal despite staying under 200KB is usually caused by non-size validation errors: (1) uploading a password-protected PDF file (GOAPS strictly forbids encrypted files), (2) an illegible issuing authority seal or registrar signature caused by excessive downsampling, (3) a corrupt PDF header resulting from an improper online converter, or (4) the certificate missing mandatory bilingual information. Always ensure your PDF is unlocked, unencrypted, and verified at 100% zoom before submission.
